# Store and check out every text file as LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF working
# copies, which:
#   * makes `bun run format:check` fail locally while passing in CI, since
#     Prettier expects LF and Linux runners check out LF;
#   * shows dozens of files as modified in `git status` whose content diff is
#     empty, because git knows it would rewrite them on the next checkout;
#   * puts a CR into `.husky/pre-commit`. That hook survives today only because
#     it is a single line with no shebang -- add either and the shell fails with
#     `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already LF, so this changes checkout
# behaviour only, never committed content. There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files
# that would legitimately want CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never apply line-ending conversion to binaries. `text=auto` detects these
# anyway; listing them is documentation, and insurance against a bad heuristic.
*.png binary
